`from_raw_parts`], except that a"},{"DocComment":" mutable slice is returned."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Safety"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Behavior is undefined if any of the following conditions are violated:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" * `data` must be non-null, [valid] for both reads and writes for `len * size_of::<T>()` many bytes,"},{"DocComment":"   and it must be properly aligned. This means in particular:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":"     * The entire memory range of this slice must be contained within a single allocation!"},{"DocComment":"       Slices can never span across multiple allocations."},{"DocComment":"     * `data` must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. One"},{"DocComment":"       reason for this is that enum layout optimizations may rely on references"},{"DocComment":"       (including slices of any length) being aligned and non-null to distinguish"},{"DocComment":"       them from other data. You can obtain a pointer that is usable as `data`"},{"DocComment":"       for zero-length slices using [`NonNull::dangling()`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" * `data` must point to `len` consecutive properly initialized values of type `T`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" * The memory referenced by the returned slice must not be accessed through any other pointer"},{"DocComment":"   (not derived from the return value) for the duration of lifetime `'a`."},{"DocComment":"   Both read and write accesses are forbidden."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" * The total size `len * size_of::<T>()` of the slice must be no larger than `isize::MAX`,"},{"DocComment":"   and adding that size to `data` must not \"wrap around\" the address space."},{"DocComment":"   See the safety documentation of [`pointer::offset`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [valid]: ptr#safety"},{"DocComment":" [`NonNull::dangling()`]: ptr::NonNull::dangling"},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"Untagged":{"data":{"file_